{
    "swagger": "2.0",
    "info": {
        "description": "This is the official, publicly accessible, API to get data in Typical Developers' experiences.\n# Notes\n- All dates and timestamps are returned in [ISO8601](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format and are set as a UTC timezone.\u003cbr\u003e\n---\n# Caching\nAll responses will return an `ETag` header, which is an MD5 hash of the response. You are able to use this hash to verify\nif there's updated content by supplying a `If-None-Match` in the requests header for the next request you make.\u003cbr\u003e\n- Status `200 - OK` will be returned if the resource has been updated.\n- Status `304 - Not Modified` will be returned if the resource has not been updated.\n---\n# Ratelimits\n\u003e [!NOTE]\n\u003e If you are constantly hitting ratelimits and need help, reach out in our community development channels in our [Discord Server](https://discord.gg/typical).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c!----\u003e\n| Duration | Requests |\n|----------|----------|\n| Daily   | Unlimited |\n| Per Minute    | 120 |\n| Per Second    | 6  |\n\u003c!----\u003e\n## Headers\n`X-RateLimit-Limit`:     The total amount of requests that can be made.\u003cbr\u003e\n`X-RateLimit-Remaining`: The remaining amount of requests that can be made before the rate-limit is exhausted.\u003cbr\u003e\n`X-RateLimit-Reset`:     The remaining amount of time for when the rate-limit resets.\u003cbr\u003e=",
        "title": "Typical Developers - Public Experience API",
        "contact": {}
    },
    "paths": {
        "/v1/oaklands/economy/stock-market/ores": {
            "get": {
                "description": "Fetch the current ore stock market.",
                "tags": [
                    "Oaklands"
                ],
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "type": "string",
                        "description": "ETag to validate cached response.",
                        "name": "If-None-Match",
                        "in": "header"
                    },
                    {
                        "enum": [
                            "name",
                            "current_multiplier",
                            "last_multiplier",
                            "values.current_value",
                            "values.base_value"
                        ],
                        "type": "string",
                        "default": "current_multiplier",
                        "description": "The field to sort by.",
                        "name": "sort_by",
                        "in": "query"
                    },
                    {
                        "enum": [
                            "desc",
                            "asc"
                        ],
                        "type": "string",
                        "default": "desc",
                        "description": "The direction to order by.",
                        "name": "order_by",
                        "in": "query"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "OK",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "data": {
                                    "type": "array",
                                    "items": {
                                        "$ref": "#/definitions/Oaklands.V1.StockMarket"
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "429": {
                        "description": "Too Many Requests",
                        "schema": {
                            "$ref": "#/definitions/API.ErrorResponse"
                        }
                    },
                    "500": {
                        "description": "Internal Server Error",
                        "schema": {
                            "$ref": "#/definitions/API.ErrorResponse"
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
